	<key>readme</key>
	<string># Grammar

LLM-powered grammar &amp; orthography checker for non-native English speakers. Fix text without changing its meaning, and learn why each change was made.

## Triggers
- **Hotkey** `⌃⌘G` (Control+Command+G) on your clipboard: copy any text, hit the hotkey, get the fix.
- **Keyword** `grammar &lt;text&gt;`: type inline to compose and check.

Both share the same provider + model config.

## Result
- `✏ corrected text` — press `↵` to copy, then `⌘V` back into your app. Subtitle shows what changed.
  - `⌘↵` copies the explanation instead.
- `💡 explanation` — press `⇧` (Shift) for the full note in your language (Quick Look).

## Setup (Workflow Configuration)
Fill these in `Configure Workflow…`:

| Variable | Example | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `Provider` | `OpenAI` *(dropdown)* | Pick from the list. Select “Custom URL” for your own endpoint. |
| `Custom Endpoint` | `https://my-proxy.com/v1/chat/completions` | Only used when Provider = “Custom URL”. |
| `API Key` | `sk-...` / `AIza...` | Required for cloud providers. Not needed for `ollama` or a local URL. |
| `Model` | `gemini-2.5-flash` | Leave blank for the provider's default (cheap/fast current tier). |
| `Explanation Language` | `Spanish` | Language of the explanation note. |

## Provider dropdown
`OpenAI` · `Anthropic Claude` · `Google Gemini` · `xAI Grok` · `DeepSeek` · `Alibaba Qwen` · `Moonshot Kimi` · `Xiaomi MiMo` · `MiniMax` · `Z.ai GLM` · `OpenRouter` · `OpenCode Go` · `Ollama (local)` · `Custom URL`

Defaults are 2026-current cheap tiers (verified via models.dev); `gemini-2.0-flash` is shut down.

Requires `jq` and `curl`: `brew install jq curl`

**GitHub**: https://github.com/EstebanForge/grammar-alfred</string>
